Z||000044||LZeitgeist||09-08-2001||07:25 PM||||No, I didn't realize the Bonnie was FWD for that long.. this is the first year that they've caught my eye, and due to the size of it, I just sorta figured it was RWD...<P>Dammit.<P>Dammit dammit dammit.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - '1982 to Present' - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000045||Mach10||09-08-2001||08:59 PM||||This one guy I work with has a buddy with a white 87 CRX. Supercharged B18 motor up front. Hood chopped open to clear. He runs high 13s consistantly. Why? first clue is that he looks like a stage rocket through 3 gears. His wheels do not bite. When he plants the gas, the car's front end jumps up OFF the pavement. <BR>FWD is not happy when you are pushing a lot of power to it. You got engine torque pushing the wheels up, AND you got the acceleration moving the weight to the back. Yes there are 9 second hondas. Slap a RWD conversion (yeah, right) and watch how much better those cars would run.||||reg||7
Z||000046||Black88GT||09-08-2001||10:06 PM||||FWD wheel stands? LMAO!!!  <P>All I can say is, I am no engineer, but when you see that even the import super cars are RWD (Supra, RX7, MR2 etc.) then that should tell you something right there. <P>You could argue the BMW M5 is the best all around car in the world.  RWD.  <P>Only thing better is AWD which adds a lot of weight.  Except if your talking about a Diablo VT that is.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000047||Master_Sushi||09-10-2001||12:15 PM||||Well, front wheel drive in winter is easier to drive in. Weight transfer isn't an issue between FWD/RWD in low traction becuase not enough acelloration. BUT, with FWD in low traction you do have to weight over the wheels. Which does help allot. In normal summer conditions RWD is allways better. Most americans don't know how to drive well anymore, so they prefer FWD because its easier to control if you don't know what the hell your doing. Front wheel drive is also WAY cheaper to build, this is a fact. I lost all faith in GM when they killed the Caprice/Impala SS. Now I hear they are cuting the F-Bodys. GM pretty much sucks now.||||reg||1
Z||000048||rogergarrison||09-10-2001||12:31 PM||||out of those 2 (fwd and rwd with front engine) drag racing rwd hands down. for speedway or road courses rwd. When was the last time you saw a fwd stock car or sports car racer. There are a few awd, but that wasnt a choice. Like said earlier, mid engine / rwd is the very best of both. Look at any rail dragster/GT/GT touring/GTP.||||reg||1
Z||000049||JohnnyK||09-10-2001||01:35 PM||||In all due respect, Front engine/rear drive is considered the best by most car engineers because of it's weight balance.||||reg||1
